cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Quantum Anchor Protocol: Frequency-Domain Wave-Packet Encoding with Hardware-Validated Quantum Bridge"
abstract: >-
  Quantum Anchor Protocol encodes a frequency-domain wave packet into quantum
  interference circuits. This release adds a hardware-validated quantum bridge:
  the encoding was measured on a real 156-qubit superconducting QPU (IBM
  ibm_marrakesh, 2000 shots per run, 2026-10-06), reaching 99.3% Bell balance
  on two qubits, 98.8% on a reproducibility run, and an ideal three-qubit GHZ
  distribution. The decoding formulas' assumption P(q0=1)=sin^2(theta/2) is
  therefore measurement-verified rather than assumed.

  Tesseract-V3 5-phase interferometric sweep on IQM Garnet (20Q, Starter tier):
  5 phases, 1024 shots each (5120 total). Wilson 95% CIs: [0.74, 2.16],
  [0.10, 0.86], [0.05, 0.71], [0.82, 2.28], [0.10, 0.86] (%). Aggregate:
  0.684% [0.49%, 0.95%]. Chi2 vs cos(8φ): 0.83 (df=4), p=0.93 — does NOT reject.
  Chi2 vs flat: 1.98 (df=4), p=0.74 — does NOT reject. Cos(8φ) fit: offset=0.684%,
  amplitude=0.511% (theory: 1.56%, 3x smaller), R^2=0.48. Evidence grade: F
  (Noise-dominated — NO phase discrimination). Pulse-level anchor drive blocked
  by IQM Starter tier (pulse access denied).

  Classical and hardware proofs are reported as strictly separate evidence
  levels. Negative results reported honestly.
type: software
